{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946606-yantras-how-the-heck-to-you-get-them","id":946606,"title":"Yantras - how the heck to you get them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T18:25:08-07:00","id":946606,"title":"Yantras - how the heck to you get them?","content":"I understand how Yantra's work, but I can't seem to find the rules regarding how one initially gains them (aside from Mudras and High Speech), or how one adds semiotic associations to a Yantra that one already possesses. Could someone point me to the actual location in MtA 2e where this is spelled out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 08-08-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:30:32-07:00","id":946612,"title":"","content":"I have troubles parsing the question. Could please provide an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:36:09-07:00","id":946619,"title":"","content":"So, what I'm understanding is that you're asking how a given object or symbol becomes a Yantra? Apart from a Dedicated Tool, you don't really do much of anything to a Yantra, it just is.<br /> <br /> A Yantra is a Yantra because it is a stand-in for a Supernal Symbol. It holds symbolism that has been recorded by Awakened and Sleepers throughout the centuries. A Mage can pick up just about anything with suitable symbolism and it becomes a Yantra, but it needs the appropriate symbolism. Not all Yantras work for all Arcana or even all spells in a given Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:18:34-07:00","id":946665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946606-yantras-how-the-heck-to-you-get-them?p=946612#post946612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have troubles parsing the question. Could please provide an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I buy (or get for free from an order) the High Speech Merit, now I can use High Speech as a + 2 Yantra via chanting.<br /> <br /> I learn a rote w/ appropriate Mudras, and can use that as a bonus to spells based on my level in the appropriate ability.<br /> <br /> I have a stick I can wave around like a symbol of authority, and if I point at things while casting, it gives me +1 to magic that compels obediance / enforces my will on another creature. How did I get it? In game terms, what determines how many Yantras I can have (not how many I can use at once, I understand Gnosis determines that)?. Is the storyteller expected to accept anything I can lay my hands on as a Yantra, as long as I can give what he determines to be a decent description on the fly of the symbolism I see in it? Can any mage standing near a stream use the purifying symbolism of water to aid in healing spells? The Yantra description, including the phrase about a mage &quot;connecting her supernal understanding&quot; to a different application of her environmental yantra, gave me the impression that there was some sort of ritual requirement to set something up as a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:33:22-07:00","id":946674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946606-yantras-how-the-heck-to-you-get-them?p=946619#post946619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what I'm understanding is that you're asking how a given object or symbol becomes a Yantra? Apart from a Dedicated Tool, you don't really do much of anything to a Yantra, it just is.<br /> <br /> A Yantra is a Yantra because it is a stand-in for a Supernal Symbol. It holds symbolism that has been recorded by Awakened and Sleepers throughout the centuries. A Mage can pick up just about anything with suitable symbolism and it becomes a Yantra, but it needs the appropriate symbolism. Not all Yantras work for all Arcana or even all spells in a given Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I need to refresh more often.<br /> If I understand you, then the determination that something is a Yantra that a player can use, and how he can use it, is largely a role playing concern. Only the bonus and number of Yantras that you can use is determined by a game mechanic. That is not the impression I got by the Yantra description, but it would explain why I can't find any mechanics.<br /> I've been mistaken before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T20:31:19-07:00","id":946712,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's pretty much how it works. There are ways to figure out what would make an appropriate Yantra, Prime Mage Sight for example picks Yantras out. Usually, a Mage probably has a good idea via his Order what will and won't make acceptable Yantras, and any Mage probably has a tendency to collect ones they know work for whatever type of spell they're going to cast. That doesn't really matter at low levels of Gnosis though since things like High Speech, Runes, Mudras, Order Tool, and Dedicated Tool pretty much have you covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T20:32:15-07:00","id":946714,"title":"","content":"So you want page 327 of our mage book with the handy yantra chart that lists the types of yantras available. Things like Patron tools, Persona and Mundra (high speech) are each their own merits and you should look at those descriptions. You can find detailed explanation of Yantras beginning on p 119. I basically skipped looking at this until I had a firm grasp on the rest of the magic system. <br /> <br /> The basic idea behind Yantras is they are any tangible (or sometimes intangible) thing that helps the mage do magic. Chanting in High speech or using Runes in High speech are examples of this. So is wielding a staff to direct a bolt of lightning. For that matter a print out of today\u2019s Doppler radar readings can be used to direct the same bolt of lightning (for a Free Council mage). The staff is a path tool, the Doppler print out is an order tool. A mage who chooses Thor as his magic Persona (with the merit) can use those merit dots in that persona to call down lightning. So a free council mage named \u201cThor\u201d who passes a staff over a map of the city overlaid with today\u2019s Doppler map could get up to +6 on a spellcasting roll to call lightning down on whatever hapless target he has selected.<br /> <br /> The dedicated magical tool is a bit more involved. Any staff made of the right materials (p 121) can serve as a path tool. Today\u2019s Doppler print out can be hot off the press but one\u2019s dedicated magical tool has to be something special to the mage in question. In the case of \u201cThor\u201d it could be that \u201cThor\u201d was a construction worker and had a favorite sledge hammer in his hand on the day that he got struck by lightning and awakened. That sledge hammer takes a great deal of time and effort to replace if it gets lost or destroyed because \u201cThor\u201d has to rebuild a connection to another hammer. That hammer as a dedicated magical tool serves as a channel for the Supernal truth of THOR\u2019S magic enabling \u201cThor\u201d to call down lightning or work any other magic with less interference from the abys (-2 paradox die).<br /> I hope this helps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous","name":"Servanous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T20:51:51-07:00","id":946718,"title":"","content":"You just kinda grab something, and if it's appropriate to your spell, your Path, and/or the situation? It's a Yantra. There's no special roleplaying concern for most of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T02:19:29-07:00","id":946820,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar168_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"168\" data-vbnamecard=\"168\">Aiden</a> basically said :P<br /> <br /> I had a player who wanted to increase the energy of the people in a classroom, so she cast a &quot;Power Spell&quot; using the symbolism in an energy bar and a coffee mug to gain a +2 bonus (+1 for each tool Yantra). The book is riddled with these kinds of examples, especially at the locations <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3741\" data-vbnamecard=\"3741\">Servanous</a> pointed out. If you want, I am sure we can give you some more examples if you want <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","user":"Neros","date":". 08-10-2016, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:13:10-07:00","id":947444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946606-yantras-how-the-heck-to-you-get-them?p=946820#post946820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar168_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"168\" data-vbnamecard=\"168\">Aiden</a> basically said :P<br /> <br /> I had a player who wanted to wanted to increase the energy of the people in a classroom, so she cast a &quot;Power Spell&quot; using the symbolism in an energy bar and a coffee mug to gain a +2 bonus (+1 for each tool Yantra). The book is riddled with these kinds of examples, especially at the locations <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3741-servanous\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3741\" data-vbnamecard=\"3741\">Servanous</a> pointed out. If you want, I am sure we can give you some more examples if you want <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm good with the concept - my issue was just that I have been laboring under the assumption that each yantra is something you basically have to learn, like a merit. They work very differently than thought.<br /> Thanks to everyone for the clarifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:46:38-07:00","id":948241,"title":"","content":"This discussion comes as a great relief for me. When I first read of yantras in the previews I had images of desperate mages going McGyver, searching for paper clips, shoe laces or what have you around them to use as yantras on the fly, or more thoughtful mages traveling to places like Stonehenge, the Pyramids or just to a lightning blasted tree deep in the woods to cast their rituals, or seeking out that rare item, a Mickey Mantle trading card, powdered black rhino horn, the hand of a murderer executed twice, then I read the section on Legacies and how they teach members new yantras and I found myself wondering if characters would be limited to only a few known yantras that they could use, giving everyone a Six-Demon-Bag (toolkit) that they carried around and that was it. As ST I much prefer the idea of my players trying to argue why ABC gum can be used to boost Life spells, then just pulling out set item number three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:28:49-07:00","id":948272,"title":"","content":"You can do it that way, but I think you'd get more bang for your buck if you made the discovery of Yantras more meaningful. On the one hand, they are kind of grab bag, Paths have materials and tools that they can freely incorporate as Yantras, and Orders and Legacies have training in using particular other Yantras, and a Mage can develop an object into a Dedicated Tool to be used as a Yantra, but moving beyond that should be a discovery process. Imagine it as being similar to an archmage seeking out a particular Quintessence. They might have an intuitive understanding of the kinds of things that might work, but not everything will and some will only work for particular spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:18:07-07:00","id":948372,"title":"","content":"My first inclination is to make the grab bag yantras the +1 reach variety, with +2 &amp; +3 saved for rarer and/or more meaningful discoveries. I disagree with the idea of 'environment' yantras, like Stonehenge, being limited to +1. First they are totally non portable and second, such valuable places will be under the control of equally powerful mages not inclined to share. Gaining access long enough to perform a ritual (or getting away after an instant casting) should be a quest in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T00:21:32-07:00","id":948417,"title":"","content":"I want to point we can have literally Prime spell that just highlights you nearest Yantras, like in adventure video game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:57:49-07:00","id":948452,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it doesn't tell you what they're good for. In my kind it just flares for materials and objects of the Path, the Obrimos' Order, and locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T18:31:27-07:00","id":948983,"title":"","content":"I'm not real keen on Prime sight myself. I want my players to come up with the ideas and arguments to justify them, Prime sight feels like we're back to me dolling everything out like multiple choice. I haven't gotten to play with the 2ed rules yet, we are still finishing our previous chronicle, but in some ways I wish they had just gone with something else like recognizing deliberate falsehoods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T18:42:14-07:00","id":948993,"title":"","content":"It's all about how you handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:09:45-07:00","id":949082,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing you could do is change it so it shows things that have been used as yantras already, perhaps even going so far as to show potential ones people have used before. (&quot;Oh, indeed, he has user a terrifying roar-like shout as a yantra at some point, hm, better be prepared if he seems to be about to do something like that...&quot;)<br /> <br /> While it would be only a minor change to the rules it would make a huge difference in play. I mean, if someone mostly has almost exclusively used martial or terrifying yantras for their magic... well, that says something about them. Would also allow you to detect the presence of mages in an area, in a roundabout way, by seeing the things they've used.<br /> The lamppost, with it's light, was used as a yantra perhaps... maybe almost all the lampposts in the outskirts of a city, all in one particular area, have been... who did it and what is it they keep casting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T04:39:52-07:00","id":949236,"title":"","content":"I ran the prime sight like this: If you have the Sight active when you cast a spell, any possible Yantras that are in line of sight becomes outlined/flares up/gives off a pulse. You can't use it in that instance of the casting, but from now on, you know that it can be used for that spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:11:49-07:00","id":949268,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much just like <u><b>stunting</b></u> from other Onyx Path games.<br /> <br /> The character grabs something that seems like it thematically fits the spell/paradigm she is trying to cast, the player makes her case, and the storyteller tosses her some free dice. How many dice are up to the Storyteller, but usually +1 unless the yantra is rare or special somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T07:45:21-07:00","id":949307,"title":"","content":"If that were the case there wouldn't be a point to Prime highlighting Yantras. I don't think that Yantras are a free for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:08:30-07:00","id":949377,"title":"","content":"Here's looking forward to 'Signs of Sorcery'. There are so many things to clarify without adding new stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T11:29:30-07:00","id":949439,"title":"","content":"In the section on place Yantras it says that the place can't be used because of the Mage's personal connection to it, but because of its meaning to Sleepers because they unconsciously reflect the Supernal attributes of the place. I would use that logic for all Yantras not directly tied to Path, Order or High Speech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:51:04-07:00","id":950698,"title":"","content":"So what you're saying is that for an Arrow a sword is a yantra because their order teaches that weapons have supernal significance, but for everyone else the Spear of Destiny would be a tool because of its place in Christian folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:34:01-07:00","id":950865,"title":"","content":"More like, any Mage can benefit from Excalibur, but Arrows can find the symbolism of Excalibur in any sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:22:35-07:00","id":950883,"title":"","content":"Arrow can use Excalibur as both a Excalibur yantra, and as a sword yantra - and if equipped with Adamant hand, as a &quot;I chopped his head off with Excalibur&quot; yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T21:16:49-07:00","id":950902,"title":"","content":"So would you value Excalibur as a +2 or a +3 yantra? What about the Spear of Destiney? What spells or Arcanum would they benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T00:45:30-07:00","id":950969,"title":"","content":"It'd just be +1. +2 if destroyed as a sacrament. +3 if you went into another realm to get them as a sacrament. More if it fits into the Cabal Theme or Shadow Name merit. Whether a Moros Yantra is lead or diamond, it's still only worth +1. I don't see why it would be different for a regular sword versus Excalibur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:29:55-07:00","id":950997,"title":"","content":"Deciding what spells they'd be useful for would be up to the ST. Like. Excalibur might be good for cutting, fighting and inspiring awe or fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T05:04:46-07:00","id":951048,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946606-yantras-how-the-heck-to-you-get-them?p=950883#post950883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arrow can use Excalibur as both a Excalibur yantra, and as a sword yantra - and if equipped with Adamant hand, as a &quot;I chopped his head off with Excalibur&quot; yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Warning: Gory<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M5QAmMCkx1Q\" data-code=\"M5QAmMCkx1Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/M5QAmMCkx1Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Look at all those yantras.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T05:33:48-07:00","id":951056,"title":"","content":"Our group is currently going with the defined magical tools version of the Yantra rules, but I can definitely see room for some houserules to encourage MaGuyvermancers to do their thing - off the top of my head, I would probably say a Mage could use anything with symbolic resonance to the Imago by flooding it with their nimbus costing a point of mana, with a dedicated merit to do it without that charge being, I dunno, 1-2 dots. Maybe doing that takes an instant action, maybe it doesn't. Season to taste.<br /> <br /> Edit:In fact, I would probably test out a version in a game I was running where every mage can flood an ad hoc yantra with their Nimbus for free as an instant action and reflexively for one mana. This allows for that tried and true scene where a mage draws a pentagram in chalk and then lays hands on it until it glows with power. (Make it obviously magic? Hmm.) <br /> <br /> If you wanted to add a restriction to emphasize defined tools, maybe the free instant action is once a scene, and maybe the dedicated merit lifts that restriction. I don't know, I'm still spitballing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 08-15-2016, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T05:37:41-07:00","id":951057,"title":"","content":"Prime 4 could probably Pattern anything into being a Yantra. Prime 3 might be able to make a sort of Yantra Wonderful Machine, taking traits of different Yantras and smashing them together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:06:13-07:00","id":951230,"title":"","content":"I think about making Human Blood as universal Yantra +2 - yours is easier to get, easily, but it gives you Bashing damage or Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}